# DURABLE REPRO — the `W_CompoundYieldRace` warning goes SILENTLY MISSING when
# the yield point sits inside a child-bearing expression in the compound
# assignment's RHS. A missing diagnostic on a genuinely racy program: nothing
# turns red, nothing is printed, the race ships.
#
# MECHANISM: `expr_contains_yield_point` in `src/semantic/safety/helpers.rs`
# hand-rolls its recursion over 20 of the 45 `Expr` variants and ends in
# `_ => false`. Any child-bearing variant among the other 25 hides the call
# from the walk, so the `&&` in `check_compound_assign`
# (`src/semantic/safety/check_stmt.rs`) never fires.
#
# THE SET, not a selection (regenerate: diff the `Expr::` names in
# `expr_contains_yield_point`'s match against
# `awk '/^pub enum Expr \{/,/^\}/' src/parser/ast.rs`).
# 16 of the 25 unhandled variants are child-bearing and therefore hiding places:
#   Block · Catch · DictComprehension · DictLiteral · Do · DotShorthand ·
#   ListComprehension · Match · MetaOpInfix · Range · Rethrow ·
#   SetComprehension · Spawn · SpawnBlocking · StringLiteral · StructLiteral
# The other 9 are genuine leaves (BoolLiteral, FloatLiteral, Identifier,
# IntLiteral, MetaOpToken, NoneLiteral, Path, ReturnValue, SelfExpr).
# ⚠ `Expr::Closure` is a DELIBERATE `false` ("closures execute separately") and
# must stay one; rule its disposition explicitly with the conversion rather
# than letting the exhaustive enumeration silently flip it.
#
# This is the SIBLING CONSUMER of the purity walker R44 Track E fixed: that
# round routed `purity_walk_expr` through the one exhaustive child enumeration
# so `fn_purity` stops lying, and this second walker on the SAME warning path
# was left hand-rolled. The two axes are independent — Track E's fixtures cover
# "which variant hides the call inside the CALLEE's body"; this one covers
# "which variant hides the call in the RACY ASSIGNMENT'S OWN RHS".
#
# AXIS = the `Expr` variant wrapping the effectful call in the RHS.
#   `ctrl` — bare `Call`               → the CONTROL. Warns today (live test).
#   `lc`   — `ListComprehension` body  → SILENT. WRONG.
#   `fs`   — `StringLiteral` interp    → SILENT. WRONG.
#   `dl`   — `DictLiteral` value       → SILENT. WRONG.
# Cells NOT sampled, and why: the other thirteen child-bearing variants share
# the same `_ => false` arm and the same one-line remedy (route this walker through
# `parser::visitor::visit_expr_children`, exactly as Track E did for
# `purity_walk_expr`); three costumes are enough to pin the class, and a
# variant-complete net arrives with the conversion.
#
# MEASURED AT HEAD (`gg check`, rc 0, stderr read from a FILE not a pipeline):
#     exactly ONE `compound assignment reads shared ...` warning — for `ctrl`.
# CAUSATION PROVED by break-and-watch: adding `ListComprehension` /
# `StringLiteral` / `DictLiteral` arms to `expr_contains_yield_point` and
# rebuilding makes ALL FOUR warnings fire; restoring drops back to one.
#
# CORRECT BEHAVIOUR (what the `#[ignore]`d tests assert): all FOUR assignments
# warn. Every one of them reads the shared variable, calls a `HasSideEffects`
# function that may release the `with` token, then writes the stale value back.
#
# ⚠ NON-CONSTANT BY CONSTRUCTION: the comprehension bound and the dict key are
# `v.len()` on a heap `Vector`, never a literal, so no present or future
# const-folder can elide the wrapping expression and accidentally green a cell.
#
# `hidden()` is `HasSideEffects` because it calls the extern builtin `print`
# (`src/semantic/purity.rs::calls_extern`). NOTE for whoever edits this file:
# `sleep` — which the lib-level tests in `src/semantic/safety/tests.rs` use —
# does NOT resolve at the CLI (`error[E_UndefinedName]`), so it cannot be used
# in a `gg check` fixture.
#
# Filed in TODO.md; graduates to a live fixture (un-ignore the three tests)
# the round `expr_contains_yield_point` is routed through the chokepoint.

int hidden():
    print("effect")
    return 1

async void worker(int &counter):
    counter = counter + 1

async void main():
    Vector[int] v = [1]
    shared int ctrl = 0
    shared int lc = 0
    shared int fs = 0
    shared int dl = 0
    Task[void] t0 = spawn worker(&ctrl)
    Task[void] t1 = spawn worker(&lc)
    Task[void] t2 = spawn worker(&fs)
    Task[void] t3 = spawn worker(&dl)
    with ctrl:
        ctrl = ctrl + hidden()
    with lc:
        lc = lc + [hidden() for i in 0..v.len()].len()
    with fs:
        fs = fs + f"{hidden()}".len()
    with dl:
        dl = dl + {v.len(): hidden()}.len()
    t0.await()
    t1.await()
    t2.await()
    t3.await()
    print(ctrl + lc + fs + dl)
